Z||000000||beachbomb||11-22-2000||10:49 AM||||Well, after much pain, time and investigation, i finally got in touch with someone who knew about the three 1989 Fiero's sitting in a lot in Detriot MI! See web site  <A HREF="http://www.pontiworld.com.au/newsletter/july2000/page2.html" TARGET=_blank>www.pontiworld.com.au/newsletter/july2000/page2.html</A> <BR>anyway, i asked him if these were for sale, as i would have bought one or all three(since they are '89's) he e-mailed me back with the following: quote "Sad to say, those cars have been scrapped. Even if they hadn't, GM would never sell'em, sorry" unquote. So if this is true, those cars are now gone, it seems kind of wierd to me that these cars sat in this lot since 1989 and now that some-one starts asking questions about them, now they are "scrapped", if true its a sad day for Fiero lovers, insanely rare cars are now gone, Moment of silence!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>Now that i've depressed everyone(sorry), have a good Holiday..Jim('84 Indy)||||reg||8
Z||000001||Julian||11-22-2000||11:52 AM||||Dude... I work at Ford & we too build pre-production vehicles. Using non production tooling & parts. Prototypes basicly for crash tests, press releases, dyno tests etc. Once we finish with them we buy them for a dollar & use them as pool cars for staff. After a year or so we get next years cars & SCRAP these!....That's right SCRAP... CRUSH..<BR>(of course I steel as much as I can such as Shift knobs, radio, yadda yadda yadda...<BR>Can you picture a 2000 Mustang Cobra getting scrapped? It's a liability issue. They do not want to be liable for any mechanical failures. Some time we give the cars to racing teams...track use only!<P>I'd tell you more but right now I need to sign out a Lincoln Nanigator for the weekend!...<P>ciao<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/meralogo.gif"> ||||reg||6
